  "headline": "Crown overlap does NOT break the commonality assumption. Among box-matched TPs (the arm that can see a mask failure), touching crowns and isolated crowns fail at the SAME rate -- 0.0250 +/- 0.0031 vs 0.0252 +/- 0.0008 -- and mean mask IoU differs by only 0.0055 (0.7093 vs 0.7148). 39.3% of the 25,705 GT crowns touch another, so this is not a small-sample corner. Mild confound in the honest direction: touching crowns are much LARGER (70.2 vs 44.1 px), and size correlates with mask quality, so part of the tiny deficit may be neighbour interference offset by a size advantage. Either way the effect is ~0.005 IoU, far short of the degradation the box-is-mostly-one-crown premise predicts.",
  "fail_rate_context": "Overall mask-fail rate among box-TPs is ~2.5%. masker_lab/failure_analysis.py recorded 8.5% on its cohort, but that used the 16px native-4096 beta=0 masker with a live det_t8 detector on 200 tiles -- a different model and cohort, so the two are not a like-for-like comparison and the improvement should not be quoted as a measured delta."
